Syspresent canvas
---------------------------

The canvas uses Syspresent JavaScript (Apache-2.0), OpenSysML Go/WASM
(Apache-2.0), the Go browser runtime (BSD-3-Clause), fflate 0.8.2 (MIT),
and elkjs 0.12.0 (EPL-2.0 option of EPL-2.0 OR GPL-3.0-or-later).
ELK supplies disposable layout geometry in its own browser worker. Native
OpenSysML remains the semantic authority. This canvas does not bundle the
VS Code renderer or libavoid. The static build includes LICENSE,
engine/OPENSYSML-LICENSE, engine/GO-LICENSE, notices/fflate-LICENSE,
notices/elkjs-LICENSE, the unmodified ELK API and worker source, package
metadata and lockfile. ELK source: https://github.com/kieler/elkjs/tree/v0.12.0
Published source package: https://registry.npmjs.org/elkjs/-/elkjs-0.12.0.tgz. engine/provenance.json records the exact source,
carried patch and binary hashes. build-inputs.json records browser inputs.
The reproducible engine source patch and its original base are retained in
scripts/wasm-prototype; no upstream dependency PR is needed to rebuild it.
